# Codebase guide: from one PCM chunk to a shared Qwen worker

This is a source-reading guide for the current **`qwen_stream` C/C++ implementation**. It progresses from a beginner mental model to process/thread ownership, protocol details and debugger work. [Architecture](ARCHITECTURE.md) is the concise reference; [report.md](../report.md) contains measured results.

**Scope:** production CLI/service, PCM simulator, transport, shared resumable engine, CPU native inference, storage/telemetry and dashboard. Native/prefix alternatives appear only where they explain runtime dispatch. Test programs, mock engines, synthetic-source walkthroughs, Python experiment suites and GPU implementations are excluded. The C++ WAV simulator under `src/benchmark/` is included because `load` and REST suites use it to send real audio; it is not a Python inference path.

